Make Tiny Tcl's "file" command a helper of Tcl16's (src/file.c; docs/DESIGN.md,
section 8.1).

Tcl16's Tcl_FileCmd handles the options that depend on DOS path syntax
(dirname, tail, rootname, extension), adds delete, mkdir and rename, and
passes the others (atime, executable, exists, isdirectory, isfile,
lstat, mtime, owned, readable, size, stat, type, writable) to Tiny Tcl's,
renamed TclDosFileCmd. Tiny Tcl's code for the four name options stays,
unreached.

diff -ru a/tcldosaz.c b/tcldosaz.c
--- a/tcldosaz.c
+++ b/tcldosaz.c
@@ -265,7 +265,7 @@
 
 	/* ARGSUSED */
 int
-Tcl_FileCmd(dummy, interp, argc, argv)
+TclDosFileCmd(dummy, interp, argc, argv)	/* tcl16: src/file.c's helper. */
     ClientData dummy;			/* Not used. */
     Tcl_Interp *interp;			/* Current interpreter. */
     int argc;				/* Number of arguments. */
